==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{m|gem-pro|*hlaibaz}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{m|ine-pro|*kel-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*kley-}}. Cognate with {{etyl|goh|-}} {{m|goh|hleib}} ({{etyl|de|-}} {{m|de|Laib}}), {{etyl|non|-}} {{m|non|hleifr}} ({{etyl|is|-}} {{m|is|hleifur||loaf}}, {{etyl|gmq-osw|-}} {{m|gmq-osw|lēver}}), {{etyl|got|-}} {{m|got|𐌷𐌻𐌰𐌹𐍆𐍃}}. The Indo-European root is also the source of {{etyl|grc|-}} {{m|grc|κλίβανος||baking oven}}, {{etyl|sla-pro|-}} {{m|sla-pro|*xlěbъ}} ({{etyl|ru|-}} {{m|ru|хлеб||bread}}, {{etyl|pl|-}} {{m|pl|chleb||bread}}).

